## 5) Referential Integrity (Basic)

Example:
dept must exist in department table.

```python
dept_df = spark.createDataFrame([( "IT",), ("HR",), ("Finance",)], ["dept"])

invalid_dept = df.join(dept_df, "dept", "left_anti")
invalid_dept.show()
```

---

## 6) Data Quality Summary (Mini Report)

```python
total = df.count()
unique_ids = df.select("id").distinct().count()

print("Total rows:", total)
print("Unique ids:", unique_ids)
print("Duplicate rows:", total - df.dropDuplicates().count())
```

---

## 7) Best Practices

✅ Always run null + duplicate checks  
✅ Keep DQ logs in a separate Delta table  
✅ Fail pipeline if critical checks fail  
✅ Track DQ metrics daily  
✅ Use Great Expectations in enterprise (optional)  

---

## 8) Summary

- Data quality checks are mandatory.
- Null checks + duplicates are common.
- Referential integrity ensures correct dimension mapping.

